 "beyond": "Not for the exam. Real columns are designed with Perry-Robertson or code buckling curves that include initial bow, residual stress and eccentricity. The same Euler-Bernoulli instability appears in micro-machined sensors, where a tiny compressive load shifts a resonant frequency, and in buckling of thin-walled shells, where imperfections drop the load far below the ideal value. Search next for Perry-Robertson formula, column curves, and buckling of thin-walled sections."
